---
// Lesson 7.7a — Level Studio II + Cross-Playtest
// Polish + the cross-playtest ritual with the data table; semester-1 arc closes.
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>7.7a — Level Studio II + Cross-Playtest</h1>

<p class="lesson-lead">
    Yesterday you built it; today strangers meet it. Polish the two
    beats that most need it, then run the cross-playtest — different
    partner, full cave, numbers on paper. This closes the level arc
    of the semester: next stop, the boss.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Studio Brief</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~25 min</span>
    </div>

    <p><strong>Polish pass — exactly two beats.</strong> From
    yesterday's walk ritual and written plan
    (<a href="7.6a.html">7.6a</a>), you know which. Polish means:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Sightlines:</strong> trim tiles until the next
            beat is glimpsed from the current one</li>
        <li><strong>Telegraphing:</strong> the threat is visible at
            rest before it is a threat (turret seen, not
            surprise-shot)</li>
        <li><strong>Reward placement:</strong> coins on the route you
            WANT walked; the coin trail is a dotted line your player
            follows without noticing</li>
        <li><strong>Death audit fix:</strong> the beat where a death
            costs the most gets either a checkpoint trigger (build
            one — it is a tag + a stored position) or a shortened
            approach</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Do NOT polish everything. Two beats, deeply. That is how
    studio time works under deadline — and your deadline is the
    cross-playtest starting in 20 minutes.</p>

    <div class="bug-hunt">
        <h3>Bug Hunt: Pre-test ritual</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Full-walk one more time, naming beats. Any NEW seams
                from polishing? Tile edits move colliders — check
                the walls you nudged.</li>
            <li>Verify from spawn: does the player know where to go
                within 5 seconds WITHOUT any instruction? What
                tells them — write the exact visual cue.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Cross-Playtest</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~25 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        New partner (not yesterday's). Silent watching
        (<a href="2.4a.html">2.4a</a> rules). Full cave, entrance to
        boss door. Record per BEAT, not per session — the beat is the
        unit of analysis (this table is the exact habit that becomes
        the dataset unit, <a href="9.5a.html">9.5a</a>):
    </p>
    <table>
        <tr><th>Beat</th><th>Deaths</th><th>Time</th><th>Tester said / did</th><th>Fix candidate</th></tr>
        <tr><td>1 Entrance</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td>2</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td>3</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td>4</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td>5</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td>6 Boss door</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
    </table>

    <p><strong>Then swap:</strong> you play THEIR cave with the same
    table. You are both designer and tester today — notice how
    different the jobs feel.</p>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Tinker: Read the numbers</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Compare the two tables (yours-as-designer vs
                theirs-as-tester). One fix only, from THEIR data.
                Apply it now — re-run that beat with them once.</li>
            <li>Look at total deaths vs your 7.5a prediction. Was
                your difficulty curve right? Where did reality
                disagree?</li>
            <li>Commit + push: <code>"7.7a: cross-playtest data + one fix"</code> — the table goes in the repo.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Polish two beats deeply: sightline, telegraph, reward route</li>
            <li>Run a beat-granular playtest and record deaths/time/quotes</li>
            <li>Apply exactly one fix from tester data and re-verify</li>
            <li>Compare your predicted difficulty curve to the measured one</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-07/index.html">Unit 7: Level Building &amp; Ladders</a> — the studio + playtest ritual</li>
        <li><a href="../data/playtests.csv">Playtest data (CSV)</a> — what collected data looks like at scale</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next: <a href="8.1a.html">8.1a — Boss Design: Spec It First</a> — Unit 8 begins.</p>
</div>`;
